-- The dedent hazard of R4. A section binder that a paste or a hand-edit pushes
-- back to column 1 stops being the section's and becomes the signature of the
-- declaration below it. Where that declaration makes no use of the name at all,
-- it is a check error that names the fix: indent the GIVEN past the §.
--
-- Only DECLARE and ASSUME are tested this way. The same test on DECIDE reports
-- five existing corpus files whose functions simply do not use one of their
-- parameters, which is indistinguishable from a dedented binder; see
-- 'detectMisattachedSectionGivens' in L4.Desugar for the measurement.

§ `S`
GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER
DECLARE Money
    HAS amount IS A NUMBER

§ `T`
GIVEN `the other rate` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `base fee` IS A NUMBER
